    "q-131231": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131231",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 6 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{24}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{24}=2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 6 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}10 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 5 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 3- & 7 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}|\\begin{aligned}10 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}10 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 11 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
