      "source_example_id": "e-8054",
      "knowledge_point": "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations",
      "kp_id": "e-8054"
    },
    "q-130879": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130879",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 & 13 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 19 & 2 & -7 & -5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 & 13 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 19 & 2 & -7 & -5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 13 & 0 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 13 & 0 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-130879-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 13 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|",
