    "q-131226": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131226",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above ${a}_{42}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries above ${a}_{42}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -16 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -16 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-131226-a",
              "type": "math",
