      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{34}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{34}=3$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{3+4}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
