    "q-91217": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91217",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{42}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{42}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-91217-a",
