    "q-91220": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91220",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-1){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-91220-a",
              "type": "math",
